{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BRAND FONTS FROM ADOBE FONTS (Corvo addition)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The brand guidelines name IvyMode for titles and IvyEpic for text. Both are served by Adobe Fonts through a "web
project". When the ID of that project is entered in the theme settings (Typography), this snippet loads its
stylesheet and points the theme's font variables at the two families. With no ID, nothing is printed and the theme
keeps the fonts chosen in the font pickers.

The web project must contain the weights used here: the title weight, the text weight and Bold (700) for text.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign adobe_fonts_id = settings.adobe_fonts_id | strip -%}

{%- if adobe_fonts_id != blank -%}
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://use.typekit.net" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://p.typekit.net" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://use.typekit.net/{{ adobe_fonts_id | url_encode }}.css">

  <style>
    :root {
      --heading-font-family: "{{ settings.adobe_heading_family | strip | escape }}", {{ settings.heading_font.fallback_families }};
      --heading-font-weight: {{ settings.adobe_heading_weight }};
      --heading-font-style: normal;
      --text-font-family: "{{ settings.adobe_text_family | strip | escape }}", {{ settings.text_font.fallback_families }};
      --text-font-weight: {{ settings.adobe_text_weight }};
      --text-font-style: normal;
    }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}
